  "notes": [
    "fix adds jinja2.sandbox.SandboxedEnvironment.wrap_str_format",
    "Three review reasons, all dead_end_chain: inspect_format_method, SandboxedEnvironment.format_string and SandboxedEnvironment.call (src/jinja2/sandbox.py). Their only resolved callers in the package end at jinja2.ext.InternationalizationExtension._install / _install_null (private, no reference) and jinja2.ext._gettext_alias (assigned to environment.globals['_'], src/jinja2/ext.py:260), so the walker found no public root. The real path is generated code: CodeGenerator.visit_Call writes environment.call(context, ...) for every template call when environment.sandboxed (compiler.py:1866), so any SandboxedEnvironment or ImmutableSandboxedEnvironment rendering a template with a call reaches SandboxedEnvironment.call (sandbox.py:380), which calls inspect_format_method (:388) and, for str.format / format_map, format_string (:390). getattr (:324) and getitem (:301), also changed by the fix, are reached the same way from visit_Getattr / visit_Getitem (environment.getattr / environment.getitem, compiler.py:1734, :1753) and already have walker entry points; they are re-listed so the record carries the truth file's names. The four methods are public and their own entry points. Checked against the record's tree 0871c71 (3.1.4-55-g0871c71d, first parent of the fix 48b0687, which is in 3.1.5 and not 3.1.4) on 2026-11-04."
  ],
